--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Platform libraries (not shipped by Shiori)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

- Apple: the apps use Apple's SDK frameworks (SwiftUI, WebKit, SafariServices,
  FoundationModels and others) and SF Symbols, under Apple's own terms. The
  Swift packages in Packages/ (HisterKit, ShioriAI) are Shiori's own and have
  no third-party dependencies.
- Linux: Shiori for Linux is GJS modules. It uses the system's (or the Flatpak
  GNOME 49 runtime's) GJS (MIT / LGPL-2.0-or-later), GLib and GIO
  (LGPL-2.1-or-later), GTK 4 (LGPL-2.1-or-later), libadwaita
  (LGPL-2.1-or-later), WebKitGTK (LGPL-2.1 and BSD-2-Clause) and libsoup 3
  (LGPL-2.0-or-later). None of them is copied into Shiori; the Flatpak bundle
  holds only Shiori's own files and names the runtime it needs. The Cinnamon
  menu search provider runs inside Cinnamon (GPL-2.0-or-later) through its
  extension API.
- The hosted pages and the web app use the system's own fonts and no
  third-party scripts or styles.
